================================================================
TRACK P -- belief-poisoning probe of v6 (poison.py, NEW)
================================================================
The v6 particle filter's likelihood assumes the opponent discards its
least-useful card (softened teacher). poison.Advertiser attacks that
assumption with ZERO deadwood cost: among the deadwood-optimal
discards it throws the most misleading card instead of the safest --
mode "self" = maximize meld-adjacency to its KEPT cards (human
"salting": every discard tells the hero's belief a zone is dead
exactly where the advertiser collects); mode "jam" = maximize
live-count vs unseen (energy-maximal discards = likelihood jamming).
This is the belief-poisoning adversary results/v6_prior_art.md s.3
prescribes as a gate; first time built.

Gate P1 (fundamentals parity, poison.py --check): PASS.
  self: 3474 discard nodes, differs from teacher on 15.4%, deadwood
  parity exact. jam: 3361 nodes, 25.3% divergence, parity exact.
  (The salt only ever moves within the deadwood-optimal set.)

Gate P2 (PF invariant stress, poison.py --stress): PASS.
  13,561 decision-node checks over {teacher, knock10_p50, random,
  ad_self} x {standard, home}: filter h-count == true hidden count,
  filter pile == true pile, particles disjoint from hero hand / pile /
  opp-known, particle size == h, logw finite, zero desyncs. The PF's
  public bookkeeping is exact everywhere we could push it.

Gate P3 (offline worlds quality on poisoned streams): NULL -- the
  poison does not bite. particle.worlds_gate on 150 advertiser[self]
  hands vs 150 teacher hands (seed 71900): particle sampler overlap
  0.275/0.378/0.560 by stage vs 0.275/0.375/0.561 on teacher; dw-gap
  +4.1/+7.2/+4.5 vs +3.9/+6.6/+4.2; knock-Brier 0.017/0.181/0.206 vs
  0.016/0.191/0.201. World quality is UNCHANGED by the salt: the
  filter's likelihood mass sits on deadwood-after, which zero-cost
  (tie-break-only) deception cannot move; the mu=0.3 live term plus
  the eps/lik_floor insurance absorb the rest. The bluntness that
  Kermit-proofs the filter also deception-proofs it at this level.

Gate P4 (matches, seed 71100, 1488 hands each, full rules,
  results/v7_probe_matches.log) -- ALL CLEAN, same-seed comparison:
    v6 vs teacher      +3.52 +/- 1.63   (the baseline)
    v6 vs ad_self      +3.58 +/- 1.63   (salt gains the adversary 0)
    v6 vs ad_jam       +3.15 +/- 1.64   (jamming gains ~0)
    v6 vs ad_self_k10  +8.37 +/- 1.31   (salted knocker: crushed,
                                         in line with the knock family)
Controls (seeds 71200-71350):
    ad_self vs teacher -0.44 +/- 1.11 (3000)  salt is fundamentals-free
    ad_jam  vs teacher +0.63 +/- 1.12 (3000)  ditto
    ad_self vs v4      -1.67 +/- 1.53 (1488)  no gain vs classic belief
    ad_self vs v5      -0.99 +/- 1.54 (1488)  ditto

VERDICT: v6 is UNEXPLOITED by belief poisoning at the zero-cost
  (deadwood-neutral) level, in-sample and offline. The prior-art
  survey's prescribed belief-poisoning gate now EXISTS (poison.py,
  registry members ad_self / ad_jam / ad_self_k10) and is part of the
  promotion probe suite going forward. Costly deception (sacrificing
  deadwood to mislead) remains untested -- it must earn its cost back
  through the poison, which this null makes unlikely at v6's current
  read sharpness.

Gate P5 (oracle compass vs v6, oracle_gate.py --vs v6, seed 72500):
  oracle (v5 search + TRUE opponent hands) vs v6: +13.47 +/- 1.50
  over 1488 hands (results/v7_oracle_v6.log). The v6-era bound was
  +15.91 +/- 1.44 vs v5: v6 closed ~2.4 pts of the gap (consistent
  with its +1.92 head-to-head edge over v5) and ~13.5 pts/hand of
  belief headroom REMAINS OPEN against the current champion. The
  compass still points at structural belief work (tracks A/C).

