================================================================
TRACK E -- adversarial audit of the evaluator (evaluate.py/viz.py)
================================================================

E1. FIXED -- the champion-belief gap (the documented v7 open item).
  evaluate.py now builds the v6 particle posterior from the position's
  transcript whenever history_check says COMPLETE, and falls back to
  the classic weights with an explicit reason line otherwise (both
  text and HTML report the belief source). The PF replay lands on the
  declared position or refuses: it cross-checks h vs hidden count,
  replayed hero hand vs 'me', filter pile vs 'pile', replayed pickups
  vs 'opp-known' -- catching transcript holes history_check cannot
  see (e.g. an 11-card hand whose final my-draw is missing: pile
  replay is consistent but the deal unwinds to 12 cards; verified).
  Demo of the gap it closes: pos_ex7 after the opponent's QS pickup --
  classic belief rates ALL QS-neighbors an identical 1.5x (including
  the irrelevant JS); the particle posterior concentrates on the
  actual queen picture (QD 2.2x, QH 1.9x).

E2. FOUND + FIXED -- filter-noise verdicts (single-filter tilt).
  A single 256-particle filter on a SHORT history carries spurious
  per-card reads of 1.2-1.7x uniform on ARBITRARY cards (measured on
  pos_take1_spec: top-read cards completely different across filter
  seeds while n_eff stays ~160-217). All 192 worlds inherit one
  filter's tilt, shifting candidate EV diffs coherently. Fix:
  FilterEnsemble -- 4 independent filter replications, worlds sampled
  from the mixture, displayed reads = ensemble mean (so the "likely
  holdings" panel stops presenting initialization noise as signal).
  Verified: pos_take4's spurious pre-ensemble "draw, significant" flip
  disappeared; verdict stable "take stands" at seeds 0/1/2.

E3. FOUND + FIXED -- overconfident "significant" verdicts at z=1.5.
  pos_take1_spec measured 12 times (filter seed x expert seed
  decomposition): the true draw-vs-take diff is ~+1.0 pt -- a genuine
  near-tie -- yet single runs printed anything from "draw +2.70 +/-
  1.27 significant" to "draw -2.98 +/- 1.29" (a ~4.5-SE swing across
  seeds). z=1.5 is the BOT's in-game deviation bar, correct on
  average over thousands of hands; presented as a one-shot analysis
  verdict it overstates. Fix: deviations with z < 2.5 are labeled
  BORDERLINE (seed-sensitive, confirm with --worlds 384 / --seed)
  in both text and HTML. Decisive verdicts (take2 z=4.5, ex6, ex7,
  turn3 knock z~6) are unaffected.

E4. FOUND + FIXED -- follow-up plan instability.
  pos_ex5's "then: discard X" landed on THREE different discards
  across three seeds (J-drop vs 4S vs 2C -- the follow-up node is
  nearly indifferent). The follow-up line now carries "(borderline --
  close call)" or "(statistical tie with Y)" annotations. NOTE: the
  library doc's old claim that the engine "keeps the JJ pair and
  sheds 4S" was itself one arm of this coin-flip -- corrected.

E5. FIXED -- opponent-model fidelity default.
  The promoted bot ALWAYS plays with opp_model=(knock threshold, 1.0);
  the evaluator's old default was None (opponent never knocks in
  rollouts) -- the same blind-spot class as the flat-engine 6C miss,
  silently active on any position file without an opp-model line.
  New default: (knock-max, 1.0), reported with "(default)"; explicit
  opt-out via "opp-model: none". Worlds default bumped 96 -> 192
  (the champion's final search stage).

E6. FOUND (doc rot) -- sample_turn3's documented showcase verdict
  ("declines a knock most humans would take", CLAUDE.md) does NOT
  reproduce under ANY engine: deep engine +8.60 +/- 1.34 for KNOCK,
  historical v4 flat engine at worlds 96 +11.13 +/- 2.08 for KNOCK,
  with or without opp-model. The engine now agrees with the humans.
  Library docs corrected.

E7. Library regenerated (txt+html) under the upgraded evaluator:
  sample_home_ten KNOCK (unchanged) | take1 take-stands + tie note |
  take2 DRAW significant (unchanged, the flagship position) |
